# 🤝 Behavioral Interview Practice

## Question

**How do you approach a technical problem that you have not seen before?**

### Professional Answer

> I would first gather information by asking appropriate questions and understanding the symptoms of the issue. Based on the user's responses, I would identify possible causes and start with basic troubleshooting steps. I would avoid making unnecessary changes and only make changes that I understand and am authorized to perform. After making a change, I would verify the result with the user. If the issue remains unresolved or requires higher-level access, I would document everything I have already checked and escalate the issue appropriately.

